Z||000000||wkayl||10-01-2001||10:19 AM||||On Sunday morning Mrfiero stopped over to add another brain to my no start problem.  We started out with the basics that I had already tried (coil, wiring, coil wire etc..).  He then did the unimaginable.  He pulled the computer out of his low mileage 88 GT.  It was a very good thought, but that wasn’t it either.  We started to use my 86GT as a parts swapper.  We swapped fuel and injector relays and other stuff.  So here is the answer you have been waiting for and who is the winner of the “Fiero, A Car Is Born” video.  I had switched out the dist. module, then the dist. (with the old module in it) and even taken the module down to Auto Zone to have tested.  Mrfiero and I decided to try the module out of my GT because we knew it was OK.  Ta-da!!  That was it.  And the winners are…(drum roll please)…….. Mefiero, JethroGT and MooCow.  I will get one to you Mike (aka Mrfiero) and will send a copy to you other two as soon as you send me your address via e-mail or private message.  Thanks to all for your help. Problem is that now my daughter will now be back on the streets.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/usa1017[1].gif">    <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"<p>[This message has been edited by wkayl (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||1
